WEBVTT

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:05.061
Last time
on Star Trek: Voyager...

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:06.935
Stay the course!

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:07.939
They're breaking through.

00:00:08.008 --> 00:00:08.838
We'll be dead

00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:10.705
if we don't get
the shields back up.

00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:11.937
Arm yourselves!

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:15.948
Who attacked you?

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:17.174
We don't know.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.718
We can't communicate with them.

00:00:19.786 --> 00:00:22.346
They've been attacking
us for weeks.

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:24.947
Your crew has been running
criminal experiments here.

00:00:25.058 --> 00:00:26.958
I know.
I designed them.

00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:28.551
You?

00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:30.289
That's a violation
of your programming.

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:32.558
They deleted
my ethical subroutines.

00:00:34.034 --> 00:00:37.367
It's easy to cling to principles
when you're standing on a vessel

00:00:37.437 --> 00:00:38.734
with its bulkheads intact,

00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:40.739
manned by a crew
that's not starving.

00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:43.241
It's never easy,
but, if we turn our backs

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:45.539
on our principles,
we stop being human.

00:00:45.612 --> 00:00:47.944
I'm putting an end
to your experiments,

00:00:48.014 --> 00:00:50.676
and you are hereby relieved
of your command.

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:53.878
I rerouted transporter control
to a panel in the next junction.

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:55.079
We can...

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:02.723
Bridge, they've got
the field generator.

00:01:02.796 --> 00:01:04.127
What do you mean,
they've got it?

00:01:04.197 --> 00:01:06.256
I don't know how, but
they beamed it off of Voyager.

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:08.095
We're going home.

00:01:08.168 --> 00:01:09.601
We can't let Voyager
stop us now,

00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:13.002
not when we're this close.

00:01:14.741 --> 00:01:15.708
Shields are down.

00:01:15.775 --> 00:01:17.037
Arm yourselves.

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:18.134
Get us out of here.

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:23.838
And now the conclusion.

00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:26.112
Fissures are opening, all decks!

00:01:31.758 --> 00:01:32.349
Captain!

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:40.429
Give me tactical control!

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.302
Good guess.

00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:50.774
I used a deflector pulse
to reinforce the shields.

00:01:50.844 --> 00:01:51.902
It won't hold for long.

00:01:51.978 --> 00:01:52.910
Bridge to Sick Bay.

00:01:52.979 --> 00:01:54.344
We have a medical emergency.

00:01:54.414 --> 00:01:55.346
Doctor, respond.

00:01:55.415 --> 00:01:56.347
Ensign.

00:01:56.416 --> 00:01:57.974
Casualty reports are coming in.

00:01:58.051 --> 00:01:59.211
Two dead, 13 wounded.

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:01.150
We took heavy damage
to the engines.

00:02:01.221 --> 00:02:02.188
The Equinox?

00:02:02.255 --> 00:02:03.187
They've gone to warp.

00:02:03.256 --> 00:02:04.587
Any sign
of nucleogenic particles?

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:05.589
No.

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:06.590
Then they haven't engaged

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:07.648
their enhanced warp drive yet.

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:08.659
Keep looking for...

00:02:18.438 --> 00:02:19.564
Report.

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:21.504
The shield grid
is back in place.

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:22.734
The aliens are staying clear.

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:24.174
Are sensors picking up Voyager?

00:02:24.244 --> 00:02:25.905
It looks like they're
under attack.

00:02:29.349 --> 00:02:31.044
Maintain course.

00:04:38.578 --> 00:04:42.844
Captain, I found the Doctor's
mobile emitter on Deck 9.

00:04:42.915 --> 00:04:44.780
You might want
to take it to Sick Bay.

00:05:10.643 --> 00:05:12.042
Any sign of the Doc?

00:05:12.111 --> 00:05:13.373
I've got him right here.

00:05:16.449 --> 00:05:18.610
Please state
the nature of the...

00:05:18.685 --> 00:05:21.119
Don't bother.

00:05:21.187 --> 00:05:22.848
You should start with Chakotay.

00:05:22.922 --> 00:05:24.253
I've got him stabilized,

00:05:24.324 --> 00:05:25.916
but he's got
internal injuries.

00:05:26.059 --> 00:05:28.289
We found your emitter
on Deck 9.

00:05:28.361 --> 00:05:30.420
I was taken hostage
by the Equinox crew.

00:05:30.496 --> 00:05:32.862
I deactivated
myself to escape.

00:05:32.932 --> 00:05:34.263
Did you stop them?

00:05:34.334 --> 00:05:35.301
No.

00:05:35.368 --> 00:05:36.494
I'd ask
for a status report,

00:05:36.569 --> 00:05:38.093
but I'm not sure
I'd want to hear it.

00:05:38.171 --> 00:05:40.196
Harry's analyzing the
sound we've been hearing.

00:05:40.273 --> 00:05:42.434
He thinks it's some form
of communication.

00:05:42.508 --> 00:05:43.440
Well, I once figured out

00:05:43.509 --> 00:05:44.942
how to speak
with a Terrelian Seapod.

00:05:45.078 --> 00:05:46.807
This couldn't be
that much harder.

00:05:46.879 --> 00:05:49.313
Once I get out of Sick Bay,
I'll lend him a hand.

00:05:49.382 --> 00:05:50.940
We should all be
focusing our efforts

00:05:51.084 --> 00:05:52.108
on finding the Equinox.

00:05:52.185 --> 00:05:54.949
First things first...
we've got to stop these attacks.

00:05:55.054 --> 00:05:56.487
Our enemies aren't the aliens.

00:05:56.556 --> 00:05:58.046
They're the humans
aboard the Equinox.

00:05:58.124 --> 00:05:59.216
It's crucial that you don't...

00:06:10.136 --> 00:06:11.626
Who is it?

00:06:11.704 --> 00:06:14.264
It's Max.
I've brought you a visitor.

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:15.364
Hold on.

00:06:16.809 --> 00:06:17.776
Come in.

00:06:22.515 --> 00:06:24.415
I'm glad you're okay.

00:06:24.484 --> 00:06:27.248
I've been using this
synaptic stimulator.

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:30.687
I was just taking a stroll
along the Tenkaran Coast.

00:06:30.757 --> 00:06:32.224
You're welcome to try it.

00:06:32.291 --> 00:06:33.656
State your intentions.

00:06:34.761 --> 00:06:38.094
You know, once we get
our enhanced warp drive

00:06:38.164 --> 00:06:40.758
back on line, we'll
be on our way home.

00:06:40.833 --> 00:06:43.859
But it'll still take
months to get there.

00:06:43.936 --> 00:06:47.303
You can spend that
time in the brig, or...

00:06:47.373 --> 00:06:50.740
you can become
part of this crew.

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:52.937
I'd prefer the latter.

00:06:53.045 --> 00:06:55.809
I'd prefer the brig.

00:06:56.883 --> 00:06:58.475
You know, Janeway's
not the only captain

00:06:58.551 --> 00:07:01.111
who can help you
explore your humanity.

00:07:01.187 --> 00:07:03.985
You would be
an inferior role model.

00:07:05.057 --> 00:07:07.218
Janeway clung to her morality

00:07:07.293 --> 00:07:09.318
at the expense of her crew.

00:07:09.395 --> 00:07:12.455
Maybe you should learn
from that mistake.

00:07:12.532 --> 00:07:15.126
Her only mistake
was trusting you.

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:19.833
Take care of her wound.

00:07:34.253 --> 00:07:37.916
First-degree phaser burns,
minor lacerations.

00:07:38.024 --> 00:07:40.117
Looks like we'll have
to amputate.

00:07:40.193 --> 00:07:41.387
That was a joke.

00:07:41.461 --> 00:07:43.759
You're supposed to smile
and make a witty retort.

00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:45.627
I'm familiar with human banter.

00:07:45.698 --> 00:07:47.563
Yours is crude and predictable.

00:07:47.633 --> 00:07:49.601
You know, Seven...
can I call you Seven?

00:07:49.669 --> 00:07:51.660
We don't have
many luxuries around here.

00:07:51.737 --> 00:07:53.136
All we've got is each other.

00:07:53.206 --> 00:07:55.037
You might try letting
your shields down,

00:07:55.107 --> 00:07:56.540
or else it's going
to be a lonely trip.

00:07:56.609 --> 00:07:57.871
I'll be damned.

00:07:57.944 --> 00:08:01.436
Looks like our Doctor
left us a replacement.

00:08:01.514 --> 00:08:02.879
Seven?

00:08:02.982 --> 00:08:05.849
We are captives.

00:08:05.918 --> 00:08:07.749
I was attacked by their EMH.

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:10.846
Looks like he downloaded
you into our database.

00:08:10.923 --> 00:08:13.221
Good.
You can treat your friend.

00:08:19.432 --> 00:08:20.694
Priming the injectors.

00:08:20.766 --> 00:08:21.698
Marla to Bridge.

00:08:21.767 --> 00:08:22.699
Go ahead.

00:08:22.768 --> 00:08:23.700
We're ready.

00:08:23.769 --> 00:08:24.701
Acknowledged.

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:26.431
Infuse the enhanced warp drive

00:08:26.506 --> 00:08:28.098
with 20 isograms
of the compound.

00:08:28.174 --> 00:08:29.766
Aye, sir.

00:08:32.879 --> 00:08:34.403
Warp drive ready.

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:36.505
Engage.

00:08:42.321 --> 00:08:43.253
What happened?

00:08:43.322 --> 00:08:44.789
Power relays are off-line.

00:08:44.857 --> 00:08:46.085
They've been encoded.

00:08:50.496 --> 00:08:51.895
Give us the codes.

00:08:51.964 --> 00:08:52.896
No.

00:08:52.965 --> 00:08:54.023
If she won't give us the codes,

00:08:54.100 --> 00:08:55.499
maybe we could
extract them ourselves.

00:08:55.568 --> 00:08:57.934
Seven's cranial infrastructure
is highly complex.

00:08:58.004 --> 00:08:59.665
You'll need months
just to figure out

00:08:59.739 --> 00:09:00.933
what she had for breakfast.

00:09:01.007 --> 00:09:02.031
That's why you're gonna help us.

00:09:02.108 --> 00:09:03.040
I refuse.

00:09:03.109 --> 00:09:04.201
Do it or I'll erase
your program.

00:09:04.277 --> 00:09:05.209
Be my guest.

00:09:05.278 --> 00:09:06.210
Doctor.

00:09:06.279 --> 00:09:07.268
Don't worry.
They need me.

00:09:07.346 --> 00:09:09.007
They'd be cutting off
their holographic nose

00:09:09.081 --> 00:09:10.173
to spite their face.

00:09:10.249 --> 00:09:11.341
Now, I suggest you...

00:09:11.417 --> 00:09:14.147
All right, Doctor.

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:15.187
Now, get to work.

00:09:15.254 --> 00:09:17.154
You know what we're looking for.

00:09:17.223 --> 00:09:19.384
Very well.

00:09:19.458 --> 00:09:20.584
She'll try to resist.

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:22.127
I'll have to restrain her.

00:09:22.194 --> 00:09:23.161
Doctor.

00:09:23.229 --> 00:09:24.890
I deleted
his ethical subroutines.

00:09:25.031 --> 00:09:26.896
He'll be a little more
cooperative now.

00:09:26.966 --> 00:09:28.058
You keep me posted.

00:09:28.134 --> 00:09:29.066
Aye, Captain.

00:09:29.135 --> 00:09:30.295
This way, please.

00:09:37.677 --> 00:09:40.669
It's not exactly Shakespeare,
but it gets the point across.

00:09:40.746 --> 00:09:42.646
A small olive branch
is still an olive branch.

00:09:42.715 --> 00:09:44.512
Run this through
your translation matrix.

00:09:44.584 --> 00:09:45.676
Set your weapons down.

00:09:45.751 --> 00:09:47.275
Commander?

00:09:47.353 --> 00:09:49.253
Somebody's got to start
trusting somebody around here.

00:09:49.322 --> 00:09:50.448
Belay that order.

00:09:50.523 --> 00:09:53.287
I appreciate your optimism,
but, in this case, weapons.

00:09:54.226 --> 00:09:55.420
Ready to transmit.

00:09:55.494 --> 00:09:57.792
Drop shields,
Bridge only.

00:09:57.863 --> 00:09:58.795
Go ahead, Harry.

00:10:16.549 --> 00:10:17.573
Raise shields.

00:10:23.422 --> 00:10:26.914
If they understood our message,
they haven't responded.

00:10:26.993 --> 00:10:28.654
There's your response.

00:10:28.728 --> 00:10:30.491
Activate
another deflector pulse.

00:10:32.331 --> 00:10:34.526
Shields are holding
at 62 percent.

00:10:34.600 --> 00:10:37.091
That should buy us another
few minutes of peace and quiet.

00:10:37.169 --> 00:10:38.796
I suggest we make
the most of it.

00:10:38.871 --> 00:10:40.771
Focus your efforts on repairing
the warp drive.

00:10:40.840 --> 00:10:41.966
We've got to find the Equinox.

00:10:42.074 --> 00:10:43.132
If it's all the same to you,

00:10:43.209 --> 00:10:44.972
I'd like to take another
stab at the message.

00:10:45.077 --> 00:10:45.975
If we can reroute...

00:10:46.078 --> 00:10:47.568
They're not listening,
Chakotay.

00:10:47.647 --> 00:10:48.978
We should be tracking Ransom,

00:10:49.048 --> 00:10:50.345
not tinkering with adverbs.

00:10:52.618 --> 00:10:54.279
Want your First Officer's
advice?

00:10:54.353 --> 00:10:55.285
Allow me.

00:10:55.354 --> 00:10:58.255
Our deflector's losing power

00:10:58.324 --> 00:11:00.417
and when it fails,
we'll be defenseless.

00:11:00.493 --> 00:11:02.256
It's Voyager we should
be worrying about,

00:11:02.328 --> 00:11:03.260
not the Equinox.

00:11:03.329 --> 00:11:04.591
You'd make
a great First Officer.

00:11:04.664 --> 00:11:06.029
It's advice worth taking.

00:11:06.098 --> 00:11:08.931
Maybe so, but we have a crew
member trapped on that ship.

00:11:09.001 --> 00:11:12.300
Is this really about Seven,
or is it about Ransom?

00:11:12.371 --> 00:11:14.396
I don't know
what you're talking about.

00:11:14.473 --> 00:11:16.407
You've been known
to hold a grudge.

00:11:16.475 --> 00:11:19.740
This man betrayed Starfleet,
he broke the Prime Directive

00:11:19.812 --> 00:11:21.575
dishonored everything
you believe in,

00:11:21.647 --> 00:11:23.205
and threw Voyager
to the wolves.

00:11:23.282 --> 00:11:24.476
Borg, Hirogen, Malon...

00:11:24.550 --> 00:11:26.518
we've run into our share
of bad guys.

00:11:26.585 --> 00:11:27.745
Ransom's no different.

00:11:27.820 --> 00:11:28.752
Yes, he is.

00:11:28.821 --> 00:11:30.550
You said it yourself.

00:11:30.623 --> 00:11:31.590
He's human.

00:11:31.657 --> 00:11:34.387
I don't blame you
for being angry,

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:36.690
but you can't compromise
the safety of this ship

00:11:36.762 --> 00:11:38.320
to satisfy
some personal vendetta.

00:11:38.397 --> 00:11:40.092
I appreciate your candor.

00:11:40.166 --> 00:11:42.498
Now let me be just as blunt.

00:11:42.568 --> 00:11:45.093
You're right, I am angry.

00:11:45.171 --> 00:11:47.264
I'm damned angry.

00:11:47.339 --> 00:11:49.967
He's a Starfleet Captain

00:11:50.042 --> 00:11:52.237
and he's decided
to abandon everything

00:11:52.311 --> 00:11:53.505
this uniform stands for.

00:11:53.579 --> 00:11:54.511
He's out there right now

00:11:54.580 --> 00:11:56.207
torturing and murdering
innocent life-forms

00:11:56.282 --> 00:11:58.842
just to get home
a little quicker.

00:11:58.918 --> 00:12:01.716
I'm not going to stand for it.

00:12:01.787 --> 00:12:05.450
I'm going to hunt him down
no matter how long it takes,

00:12:05.524 --> 00:12:07.492
no matter what the cost.

00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:09.926
If you want to call
that a vendetta,

00:12:10.062 --> 00:12:11.654
go right ahead.

00:12:30.783 --> 00:12:31.807
Why did you bring us here?

00:12:31.884 --> 00:12:34.114
This planet has
a parthogenic atmosphere.

00:12:34.186 --> 00:12:35.813
It'll keep us
from being detected

00:12:35.888 --> 00:12:36.946
while we make repairs.

00:12:37.089 --> 00:12:38.920
We also found
a few deuterium deposits.

00:12:38.991 --> 00:12:40.390
Take an away team, Noah,

00:12:40.459 --> 00:12:42.324
and see if you can
localize the ore.

00:12:42.394 --> 00:12:43.759
You won't be protected
from the aliens.

00:12:43.829 --> 00:12:44.853
Arm yourselves with phasers.

00:12:44.930 --> 00:12:46.557
At the first sign of trouble,
we'll beam you back.

00:12:46.632 --> 00:12:47.929
Aye, sir.

00:12:49.535 --> 00:12:52.766
The ocular node's connected
to the sensory node

00:12:52.838 --> 00:12:55.739
The sensory node's connected
to the cortical node

00:12:55.808 --> 00:12:59.300
The cortical node's connected
to the reticular node...

00:12:59.378 --> 00:13:00.902
Oh, now, don't look so gloomy.

00:13:00.980 --> 00:13:03.175
There's a silver lining
to all this.

00:13:03.249 --> 00:13:06.184
Just think... we're
finally going to see Earth.

00:13:06.252 --> 00:13:08.618
You are obviously delusional.

00:13:08.687 --> 00:13:11.053
Allow me to repair
your program.

00:13:11.123 --> 00:13:13.921
Now, why would I want you
to do that?

00:13:13.993 --> 00:13:15.927
You of all people
should understand.

00:13:16.061 --> 00:13:18.359
Being unfettered
by ethical subroutines

00:13:18.430 --> 00:13:20.660
has made me far more efficient.

00:13:20.733 --> 00:13:22.166
Status?

00:13:22.234 --> 00:13:24.327
I'm going to extract
her cortical array.

00:13:24.403 --> 00:13:26.735
It contains an index
of her memory engrams.

00:13:26.806 --> 00:13:29.570
But once I've removed it,
her higher brain functions,

00:13:29.642 --> 00:13:34.909
language, cognitive skills
will be severely damaged.

00:13:42.087 --> 00:13:43.918
Tell me the codes.

00:13:43.989 --> 00:13:45.650
No.

00:13:45.724 --> 00:13:48.955
Janeway was right
about one thing...

00:13:49.094 --> 00:13:51.289
you are unique.

00:13:51.363 --> 00:13:53.957
Now, it would be a shame
to lose you.

00:13:54.099 --> 00:13:56.624
Your compassion is irrelevant.

00:13:56.702 --> 00:13:59.671
You think this is easy for me?

00:13:59.738 --> 00:14:03.071
The sight of you
on that table...

00:14:04.510 --> 00:14:06.501
But you're leaving
me no choice.

00:14:06.579 --> 00:14:09.047
"No choice."

00:14:09.114 --> 00:14:11.082
You say that frequently.

00:14:11.150 --> 00:14:14.483
You destroy life-forms
to attain your goals,

00:14:14.553 --> 00:14:17.488
then claim that they
left you no choice.

00:14:17.556 --> 00:14:19.581
Does that logic comfort you?

00:14:23.562 --> 00:14:25.052
The codes.

00:14:25.130 --> 00:14:29.624
You'll have to destroy me
to obtain them.

00:14:41.080 --> 00:14:44.914
The reticular node's connected
to the occipital node...

00:14:44.984 --> 00:14:47.282
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:14:47.353 --> 00:14:50.288
Our warp drive's back on line,
but repeated sensor sweeps

00:14:50.356 --> 00:14:52.256
have failed
to locate the Equinox.

00:14:55.060 --> 00:14:56.857
Come in.

00:14:58.330 --> 00:14:59.524
You wanted to see me?

00:14:59.598 --> 00:15:02.829
It's not like you to submit
recommendations in writing.

00:15:02.902 --> 00:15:06.030
The last time we spoke,
you weren't exactly receptive.

00:15:06.105 --> 00:15:09.040
I'm afraid I'm not going to be
very receptive this time either.

00:15:09.108 --> 00:15:11.474
It's an interesting idea,
but the Ankari

00:15:11.543 --> 00:15:13.067
are 50 light-years
in the wrong direction.

00:15:13.145 --> 00:15:15.705
I understand that,
but they're the ones

00:15:15.781 --> 00:15:17.681
who introduced Ransom
to these life-forms.

00:15:17.750 --> 00:15:18.717
It stands to reason

00:15:18.784 --> 00:15:20.718
they might be able
to communicate with them...

00:15:20.786 --> 00:15:22.219
tell them to call off
their attacks.

00:15:22.288 --> 00:15:24.848
Our first priority
is to find Ransom.

00:15:28.360 --> 00:15:31.193
Still no sign
of nucleogenic particles?

00:15:31.263 --> 00:15:32.321
Not yet.

00:15:32.398 --> 00:15:33.888
Then he couldn't
have gotten far.

00:15:33.966 --> 00:15:36.059
Without his enhanced drive,

00:15:36.135 --> 00:15:39.036
his ship's only capable
of warp 6.

00:15:39.104 --> 00:15:41.766
I've been studying
his service record.

00:15:41.840 --> 00:15:44.775
He's had his share of run-ins
with hostile aliens.

00:15:44.843 --> 00:15:47.869
It seems that when
he's being pursued,

00:15:47.947 --> 00:15:49.380
he tends to hide.

00:15:49.448 --> 00:15:52.246
At Epsilon IV he ran into
a Klingon bird-of-prey.

00:15:52.318 --> 00:15:55.651
Played a game of cat and mouse
for three days in a nebula

00:15:55.721 --> 00:15:57.712
before the Klingons
finally gave up.

00:15:57.790 --> 00:16:00.953
Two years later,
he eluded a Romulan warbird

00:16:01.026 --> 00:16:03.893
by taking his vessel
into the atmosphere

00:16:03.963 --> 00:16:05.897
of a gas giant.

00:16:06.031 --> 00:16:07.658
Go to Astrometrics.

00:16:07.733 --> 00:16:09.997
Start looking
for the kind of place

00:16:10.069 --> 00:16:12.367
you would hide
if your ship was damaged.

00:16:12.438 --> 00:16:13.405
Yes, ma'am.

00:17:03.689 --> 00:17:06.123
How was the beach?

00:17:06.191 --> 00:17:08.853
Do these programs
have people in them?

00:17:08.927 --> 00:17:10.827
No, just landscapes. Why?

00:17:10.896 --> 00:17:12.796
Forget it.

00:17:17.536 --> 00:17:19.629
I'm reading a vein of ore.

00:17:19.705 --> 00:17:23.402
Azimuth 117... 30 meters.

00:17:23.475 --> 00:17:24.772
It could run pretty deep.

00:17:24.843 --> 00:17:27.471
We might need to use
phasers to excavate it.

00:17:27.546 --> 00:17:29.912
It's funny, this reminds me
of McKinley Park.

00:17:30.015 --> 00:17:33.178
I used to take my sister there
when we were kids.

00:17:33.252 --> 00:17:34.719
This place looks just like it.

00:17:34.787 --> 00:17:37.347
As I recall, there was
a family of ground squirrels

00:17:37.423 --> 00:17:38.754
who lived right over there.

00:17:38.824 --> 00:17:40.917
And there was a patch
of poison ivy next to it.

00:17:41.026 --> 00:17:43.051
When I was 10, I walked
right through it

00:17:43.128 --> 00:17:45.323
and I swelled up like
a Regellian blood worm.

00:17:45.397 --> 00:17:46.329
When I get back to Earth,

00:17:46.398 --> 00:17:47.729
the first thing
I'm going to do is...

00:17:51.837 --> 00:17:53.395
Four to beam up.

00:17:58.844 --> 00:18:00.903
We're receiving
a subspace transmission.

00:18:00.979 --> 00:18:02.003
From who?

00:18:02.081 --> 00:18:03.013
I can't tell.

00:18:03.082 --> 00:18:04.606
I don't see a ship out there.

00:18:04.683 --> 00:18:05.672
Open a channel.

00:18:05.751 --> 00:18:08.879
Doctor to Equinox.
Respond.

00:18:08.954 --> 00:18:10.046
We can hear you.

00:18:10.122 --> 00:18:12.056
Voyager's found you.
They've entered orbit.

00:18:12.124 --> 00:18:15.116
They polarized their hull
to mask their approach.

00:18:15.194 --> 00:18:16.218
I believe they've already

00:18:16.295 --> 00:18:17.762
planned an ambush
on the away team.

00:18:17.830 --> 00:18:19.764
Janeway's been tracking
the Equinox...

00:18:21.633 --> 00:18:22.861
Get him back.

00:18:22.935 --> 00:18:24.300
I can't.

00:18:24.369 --> 00:18:26.496
Ransom to away team.

00:18:26.572 --> 00:18:29.803
Noah, prepare to beam back
to the ship.

00:18:31.143 --> 00:18:32.576
They're not down there.

00:18:37.983 --> 00:18:40.952
All hands to battle stations.

00:18:45.991 --> 00:18:47.652
30,000 kilometers and closing.

00:18:47.726 --> 00:18:49.318
Target their power core.

00:18:57.703 --> 00:18:58.761
Direct hit.

00:18:58.837 --> 00:18:59.804
Minor damage.

00:18:59.872 --> 00:19:01.066
Return fire.

00:19:03.475 --> 00:19:05.409
Bridge to Torres.
Status?

00:19:05.477 --> 00:19:07.877
I can't locate
their shield grid generator.

00:19:07.980 --> 00:19:10.107
Can you divert more power
to sensors?

00:19:10.182 --> 00:19:11.979
Stand by.

00:19:12.050 --> 00:19:14.041
They've damaged
our deflector, Captain.

00:19:14.119 --> 00:19:15.108
If it goes off-line,

00:19:15.187 --> 00:19:16.848
we'll be vulnerable
to the alien attacks.

00:19:16.922 --> 00:19:17.854
Noted.

00:19:17.923 --> 00:19:19.185
Target his weapons array.

00:19:22.161 --> 00:19:23.822
We lost our phaser banks.

00:19:23.896 --> 00:19:25.625
Torpedoes full spread.

00:19:25.697 --> 00:19:26.629
It's B'Elanna.

00:19:26.698 --> 00:19:28.791
She's trying to bypass
our security protocols.

00:19:28.867 --> 00:19:29.834
Stop her.

00:19:33.872 --> 00:19:38.241
Computer, open a com-link
to the Equinox.

00:19:38.310 --> 00:19:40.471
Workstation 33-Beta.

00:19:40.546 --> 00:19:41.638
Max, listen to me.

00:19:41.713 --> 00:19:43.442
Back for round two, BLT?

00:19:43.515 --> 00:19:45.676
This isn't one of our games.

00:19:45.751 --> 00:19:47.844
People are dying over here.

00:19:47.920 --> 00:19:49.547
I wish you didn't have
to be one of them.

00:19:49.621 --> 00:19:52.146
Max, please...

00:19:54.526 --> 00:19:55.686
Shields are weakening.

00:19:55.761 --> 00:19:56.921
We've almost got him.

00:19:56.995 --> 00:19:58.860
Keep targeting
their weapons array.

00:19:58.931 --> 00:20:00.660
One more torpedo ought to do it.

00:20:00.732 --> 00:20:02.029
Captain...

00:20:02.100 --> 00:20:03.124
Fire.

00:20:08.974 --> 00:20:10.066
Weapons are down!

00:20:10.142 --> 00:20:11.166
Janeway to Ransom.

00:20:11.243 --> 00:20:13.074
Surrender your vessel.

00:20:13.145 --> 00:20:15.238
We still have thrusters,
don't we?

00:20:15.314 --> 00:20:16.542
Aye, sir.

00:20:16.615 --> 00:20:17.946
Lay in a course

00:20:18.083 --> 00:20:20.677
through the planet's
atmosphere...

00:20:20.752 --> 00:20:22.413
60-degree vector.

00:20:28.994 --> 00:20:30.689
What the hell is he doing?

00:20:30.762 --> 00:20:31.729
Follow him.

00:20:35.167 --> 00:20:37.965
We're crossing
the upper thermosphere.

00:20:38.103 --> 00:20:39.331
Phasers.

00:20:49.681 --> 00:20:51.444
Shields are weakening...

00:20:51.516 --> 00:20:53.279
31 percent...

00:20:53.352 --> 00:20:54.512
29...

00:20:55.654 --> 00:20:58.088
Inertial dampers are off-line.

00:20:58.156 --> 00:21:02.217
Captain, if we lose our shields,
we'll be attacked by the aliens.

00:21:03.562 --> 00:21:05.655
Captain!

00:21:05.731 --> 00:21:07.699
Break off pursuit!

00:21:11.536 --> 00:21:13.197
They're retreating.

00:21:13.272 --> 00:21:14.466
Take us up!

00:21:18.744 --> 00:21:21.406
They took heavy damage...
shields, propulsion.

00:21:21.480 --> 00:21:23.141
Get us out of here.

00:21:25.117 --> 00:21:26.550
They've gone to warp.

00:21:26.618 --> 00:21:28.586
Match their course and speed.

00:21:28.654 --> 00:21:30.918
We can't, not until we restore
primary systems.

00:21:30.989 --> 00:21:31.921
Time?

00:21:31.990 --> 00:21:33.355
We'll need a few hours.

00:21:34.593 --> 00:21:37.061
At least we didn't
come away empty-handed.

00:21:47.439 --> 00:21:49.873
I want Ransom's tactical status.

00:21:49.941 --> 00:21:52.068
I want it now, Mr. Lessing.

00:21:54.880 --> 00:21:55.972
Or what?

00:21:56.048 --> 00:21:57.675
You'll hit me?

00:22:00.385 --> 00:22:01.647
No, Crewman.

00:22:01.720 --> 00:22:05.053
I'll drop the shields
around this room,

00:22:05.123 --> 00:22:09.492
and let your little friends
come pay you a visit.

00:22:09.561 --> 00:22:10.926
That would be murder.

00:22:11.063 --> 00:22:14.658
You could also call
it "poetic justice."

00:22:14.733 --> 00:22:16.325
I suppose the plan is

00:22:16.401 --> 00:22:19.336
that you're going to come
to my rescue now, right?

00:22:19.404 --> 00:22:21.338
There's no plan
as far as I know.

00:22:21.406 --> 00:22:22.839
The Captain's on her own.

00:22:22.908 --> 00:22:25.206
Ransom's status, now.

00:22:26.411 --> 00:22:28.208
No way in hell.

00:22:32.751 --> 00:22:36.243
We all make our own hell,
Mr. Lessing.

00:22:36.321 --> 00:22:38.516
I hope you enjoy yours.

00:22:38.590 --> 00:22:40.148
The com is active.

00:22:40.225 --> 00:22:41.658
We'll be outside

00:22:41.727 --> 00:22:43.695
if you have a change of heart.

00:22:52.471 --> 00:22:53.768
What are you doing?

00:22:53.839 --> 00:22:55.670
Weren't you listening?

00:22:56.975 --> 00:22:58.465
Don't do this.

00:22:58.543 --> 00:23:00.135
He'll break.

00:23:05.083 --> 00:23:06.311
Bridge to the Captain.

00:23:06.385 --> 00:23:09.252
We've lost shields
in Section 29-Alpha.

00:23:09.321 --> 00:23:10.754
I know. Stand by.

00:23:10.822 --> 00:23:12.483
He's a loyal officer.

00:23:12.557 --> 00:23:14.184
He's not going
to betray his Captain.

00:23:14.259 --> 00:23:15.317
Put up the shields.

00:23:15.394 --> 00:23:16.588
He'll break.

00:23:17.896 --> 00:23:19.056
Captain!

00:23:19.131 --> 00:23:20.792
As you were.

00:23:22.734 --> 00:23:25.168
Level nine authorization
required.

00:23:25.237 --> 00:23:26.704
Damn it, Kathryn!

00:23:26.772 --> 00:23:27.739
You're panicking.

00:23:27.806 --> 00:23:28.864
He's going to talk.

00:23:28.940 --> 00:23:32.137
Captain, a fissure
is opening in that section.

00:23:32.210 --> 00:23:33.234
Understood.

00:23:52.164 --> 00:23:55.497
Okay, you've demonstrated
your loyalty to your Captain.

00:23:55.567 --> 00:23:56.591
Fine.

00:23:56.668 --> 00:23:59.603
Now let's talk about the Ankari.

00:24:05.377 --> 00:24:06.708
If there's an Ankari vessel

00:24:06.778 --> 00:24:08.541
less than two light-years
from here,

00:24:08.613 --> 00:24:09.910
why haven't we detected it?

00:24:10.015 --> 00:24:12.506
Apparently, they use
a unique form of propulsion,

00:24:12.584 --> 00:24:14.484
which makes them hard to find.

00:24:14.553 --> 00:24:16.316
You think they'll be
willing to help us?

00:24:16.388 --> 00:24:17.878
It's worth a try.

00:24:17.956 --> 00:24:18.923
Mr. Lessing has agreed

00:24:19.057 --> 00:24:20.888
to show you
how to adjust the sensors.

00:24:20.959 --> 00:24:22.324
Once you find the Ankari ship,

00:24:22.394 --> 00:24:24.259
- set a course.
- Aye, sir.

00:24:24.329 --> 00:24:26.923
Did our prisoner disclose
any other information?

00:24:27.032 --> 00:24:28.090
I'm afraid not.

00:24:28.166 --> 00:24:30.930
The rest of you continue
with the repairs.

00:24:31.036 --> 00:24:33.061
Dismissed.

00:24:34.940 --> 00:24:35.929
Commander.

00:24:36.041 --> 00:24:38.236
All right.

00:24:38.310 --> 00:24:39.937
We're going to try it your way.

00:24:40.078 --> 00:24:42.638
But I want to make
one thing clear.

00:24:42.714 --> 00:24:44.944
Our first priority
is to get Ransom.

00:24:45.016 --> 00:24:47.177
If there's one thing
you've made clear, it's that.

00:24:48.820 --> 00:24:50.845
We've had our disagreements,
Chakotay,

00:24:50.922 --> 00:24:53.083
but you've never
openly opposed me.

00:24:53.158 --> 00:24:54.591
You almost killed
that man today.

00:24:54.659 --> 00:24:56.650
It was a calculated risk
and I took it.

00:24:56.728 --> 00:24:57.786
It was a bad call.

00:24:57.863 --> 00:24:59.626
I'll note your objection
in my log.

00:24:59.698 --> 00:25:01.427
I don't give a damn
about your log.

00:25:01.500 --> 00:25:03.468
This isn't about rules
and regulations.

00:25:03.535 --> 00:25:04.900
It's about right and wrong.

00:25:05.003 --> 00:25:06.061
And I'm warning you...

00:25:06.137 --> 00:25:08.105
I won't let you
cross that line again.

00:25:09.241 --> 00:25:11.141
Well then you leave
me no choice.

00:25:11.209 --> 00:25:15.612
You are hereby relieved of duty
until further notice.

00:25:19.784 --> 00:25:21.581
What's happened to you, Kathryn?

00:25:21.653 --> 00:25:24.213
I was about to ask
you the same question.

00:25:37.302 --> 00:25:38.564
They are not responding.

00:25:38.637 --> 00:25:40.104
Tractor beam.

00:25:40.171 --> 00:25:42.833
Captain, the Ankari ship
has done nothing to...

00:25:42.908 --> 00:25:44.205
Just do it.

00:25:47.646 --> 00:25:49.170
We're being hailed.

00:25:49.247 --> 00:25:50.646
On screen.

00:25:51.316 --> 00:25:52.943
Starfleet.

00:25:53.084 --> 00:25:54.711
Yes.

00:25:54.786 --> 00:25:55.718
Leave us alone.

00:25:55.787 --> 00:25:57.414
There's nothing of value
on our ship.

00:25:57.489 --> 00:25:58.751
We need your guidance.

00:25:58.823 --> 00:26:01.553
Your spirits of good fortune
are attacking us.

00:26:01.626 --> 00:26:03.753
Of course they are.
You've been killing them!

00:26:03.828 --> 00:26:06.319
We are not the ones responsible.

00:26:06.398 --> 00:26:08.366
Equinox.

00:26:08.433 --> 00:26:09.457
That's right.

00:26:09.534 --> 00:26:11.593
Can you communicate
with the aliens?

00:26:11.670 --> 00:26:14.400
Release my ship.

00:26:14.472 --> 00:26:15.905
I can't do that.

00:26:15.974 --> 00:26:17.942
Not until you agree
to talk to them.

00:26:19.477 --> 00:26:21.274
I will summon them,

00:26:21.346 --> 00:26:23.780
but you must talk to them.

00:26:23.848 --> 00:26:25.941
You must convince them.

00:26:39.731 --> 00:26:43.497
They say they want
the humans to die.

00:26:43.568 --> 00:26:46.833
A difficult place
to start a negotiation.

00:26:46.905 --> 00:26:48.338
Will they understand me?

00:26:48.406 --> 00:26:49.771
Yes.

00:26:49.841 --> 00:26:52.105
We didn't do this to you.

00:26:52.177 --> 00:26:54.975
We're trying to stop
the humans who did.

00:26:58.116 --> 00:27:00.812
They don't believe
you would harm your own kind.

00:27:00.885 --> 00:27:03.718
We have rules for behavior.

00:27:03.788 --> 00:27:05.813
The Equinox has
broken those rules

00:27:05.890 --> 00:27:07.357
by killing your species.

00:27:07.425 --> 00:27:09.188
It's our duty to stop them.

00:27:12.197 --> 00:27:17.225
Give us the Equinox.
Give us the Equinox.

00:27:17.302 --> 00:27:21.432
They insist on destroying
the ones who were responsible.

00:27:21.506 --> 00:27:25.567
We will punish them
according to our own rules.

00:27:27.345 --> 00:27:29.438
They will be imprisoned.

00:27:29.514 --> 00:27:31.414
They will lose their freedom.

00:27:33.385 --> 00:27:35.353
All right.

00:27:37.589 --> 00:27:41.525
If you stop your attacks,
I'll deliver the Equinox to you.

00:27:41.593 --> 00:27:42.525
Captain...

00:27:42.594 --> 00:27:43.925
I know what I'm doing, Tuvok.

00:27:43.995 --> 00:27:46.828
These beings would destroy
Captain Ransom and his crew.

00:27:46.898 --> 00:27:47.922
What's their answer?

00:27:47.999 --> 00:27:49.762
Your behavior is irrational.

00:27:49.834 --> 00:27:51.096
We could find
another solution.

00:27:51.169 --> 00:27:53.103
I've already confined
my First Officer to quarters.

00:27:53.171 --> 00:27:54.263
Would you like to join him?

00:27:54.339 --> 00:27:55.567
Well?

00:27:57.308 --> 00:27:58.605
They agree.

00:28:03.715 --> 00:28:05.273
We're going to need more fuel.

00:28:05.350 --> 00:28:08.478
We've only got enough left
to jump another 500 light-years.

00:28:08.553 --> 00:28:12.683
"Fuel"? Is that the euphemism
we're using now?

00:28:12.757 --> 00:28:15.692
You mean we need
to kill more life-forms.

00:28:15.760 --> 00:28:17.159
Several more.

00:28:23.268 --> 00:28:27.068
Oh, my darling, oh, my darling

00:28:27.138 --> 00:28:29.265
Oh, my darling...

00:28:29.340 --> 00:28:31.399
Clementine...

00:28:31.476 --> 00:28:33.103
How much longer?

00:28:33.178 --> 00:28:34.236
Another hour.

00:28:34.312 --> 00:28:35.336
Maybe less.

00:28:35.413 --> 00:28:38.473
You are lost and gone forever...

00:28:38.550 --> 00:28:41.110
Dreadful sorry, Clementine...

00:28:41.186 --> 00:28:42.483
What are you doing?

00:28:42.554 --> 00:28:44.852
Her auditory processor.

00:28:44.923 --> 00:28:46.914
We used to practice duets
together.

00:28:47.058 --> 00:28:50.152
In fact, I taught her
this old chestnut.

00:28:50.228 --> 00:28:52.219
Light she was

00:28:52.297 --> 00:28:53.491
And like a fairy...

00:28:53.565 --> 00:28:56.864
And her shoes
were number nine...

00:28:56.935 --> 00:28:59.665
Herring boxes without topses...

00:28:59.738 --> 00:29:02.866
Sandals were for Clementine...

00:29:03.007 --> 00:29:05.999
Drove she ducklings
to the water...

00:29:06.077 --> 00:29:07.271
Enough.

00:29:09.314 --> 00:29:10.872
Why the long face, Captain?

00:29:11.015 --> 00:29:14.109
You're about to get
your crew home.

00:29:14.185 --> 00:29:16.483
She tried to stand in your way.

00:29:16.554 --> 00:29:18.613
You had no choice.

00:29:18.690 --> 00:29:21.625
No choice.

00:29:21.693 --> 00:29:24.890
Thank you, Doctor.

00:29:27.031 --> 00:29:29.693
When this is all over,
perhaps you'll allow me

00:29:29.768 --> 00:29:31.326
to teach you my repertoire.

00:29:31.402 --> 00:29:33.393
I'm going to need
a new partner.

00:29:36.708 --> 00:29:38.471
Hmm.

00:29:38.543 --> 00:29:42.240
Drove she ducklings
to the water...

00:30:19.384 --> 00:30:21.511
You.

00:30:21.586 --> 00:30:23.611
What are you doing here?

00:30:23.688 --> 00:30:26.179
Hiding. Like you.

00:30:26.257 --> 00:30:28.088
I'm not hiding.

00:30:29.494 --> 00:30:30.722
It's beautiful.

00:30:30.795 --> 00:30:33.263
I can see why
this brings you comfort.

00:30:33.331 --> 00:30:35.765
I don't know
what you're talking about.

00:30:35.834 --> 00:30:37.859
But it isn't real.

00:30:37.936 --> 00:30:39.961
You're not real.

00:30:40.104 --> 00:30:42.299
Now leave me alone.

00:30:42.373 --> 00:30:44.136
It's not too late to stop.

00:30:44.209 --> 00:30:45.972
I don't have a choice.

00:30:46.077 --> 00:30:47.874
Find another way.

00:30:47.946 --> 00:30:49.607
There is no other way.

00:30:49.681 --> 00:30:50.773
Stop trying to hide.

00:30:50.849 --> 00:30:51.975
I told you! I'm not hiding!

00:30:52.050 --> 00:30:52.982
Now get away from me!

00:30:53.051 --> 00:30:54.541
End this.

00:30:54.619 --> 00:30:55.586
No!

00:31:00.592 --> 00:31:02.321
Bridge to Ransom.

00:31:05.997 --> 00:31:06.929
Go ahead.

00:31:06.998 --> 00:31:09.091
Janeway's found us.

00:31:11.703 --> 00:31:13.637
On my way.

00:31:20.011 --> 00:31:20.943
Distance?

00:31:21.012 --> 00:31:22.775
50,000 kilometers, closing fast.

00:31:22.847 --> 00:31:24.747
Maintain course.

00:31:26.217 --> 00:31:27.946
Voyager's approaching
at high warp.

00:31:28.086 --> 00:31:29.280
There's a class-2 nebula

00:31:29.354 --> 00:31:30.651
less than a light-year
from here.

00:31:30.722 --> 00:31:32.849
Janeway's sensors won't
be able to track us

00:31:32.924 --> 00:31:33.856
once we're inside.

00:31:33.925 --> 00:31:35.358
I think that we
should pursue this...

00:31:35.426 --> 00:31:36.688
No. Open a channel.

00:31:36.761 --> 00:31:37.921
Change of tactics?

00:31:37.996 --> 00:31:39.361
You might say that.

00:31:39.430 --> 00:31:41.955
It's time we found
another way home.

00:31:42.100 --> 00:31:43.533
Another way?

00:31:43.601 --> 00:31:46.729
We're going to cooperate
with Janeway, Max,

00:31:46.804 --> 00:31:49.170
if she's willing.

00:31:49.240 --> 00:31:50.969
Rudy, with all due respect,
have you lost your mind?

00:31:51.075 --> 00:31:52.702
Just the opposite.

00:31:54.779 --> 00:31:56.440
They're within range.
They're charging weapons.

00:31:56.514 --> 00:31:58.209
- Hail them.
- Belay that order.

00:31:58.283 --> 00:31:59.215
Raise shields.

00:31:59.284 --> 00:32:00.751
You're relieved of duty,
Commander.

00:32:02.387 --> 00:32:03.354
I'm taking command.

00:32:03.421 --> 00:32:06.015
Anyone who isn't with me,
speak up now.

00:32:11.095 --> 00:32:12.722
Take him to the brig.

00:32:20.138 --> 00:32:21.332
I'm sorry.

00:32:27.779 --> 00:32:29.337
What's the status
of our weapons?

00:32:29.414 --> 00:32:30.779
Full complement of torpedoes.

00:32:30.848 --> 00:32:32.873
Minimal phasers.

00:32:32.951 --> 00:32:35.317
Open a secure channel
to their Sick Bay.

00:32:35.386 --> 00:32:36.410
Stand by weapons.

00:32:36.487 --> 00:32:37.818
Aye, sir.

00:32:49.667 --> 00:32:50.929
I'm here.

00:32:51.002 --> 00:32:52.401
We going to need
your help, Doctor.

00:32:52.470 --> 00:32:54.802
See if you can find Voyager's
current shield frequency.

00:32:54.872 --> 00:32:56.863
Acknowledged.
I'll need a few minutes.

00:33:02.747 --> 00:33:04.738
They are firing torpedoes.

00:33:04.816 --> 00:33:07.182
Direct hit to our port shields.

00:33:07.251 --> 00:33:08.183
They're holding.

00:33:08.252 --> 00:33:09.412
Return the favor.

00:33:20.898 --> 00:33:21.830
This isn't the brig.

00:33:21.899 --> 00:33:22.991
I know.

00:33:25.036 --> 00:33:26.503
I'm with you, sir.

00:33:26.571 --> 00:33:28.937
Let's find a way to end this.

00:33:29.073 --> 00:33:32.565
We'll need to access
transporter control.

00:33:40.151 --> 00:33:41.778
We've damaged
their port nacelle.

00:33:41.853 --> 00:33:42.945
They're venting plasma.

00:33:43.087 --> 00:33:44.645
They're dropping out of warp.

00:33:44.722 --> 00:33:45.882
Stay with them.

00:33:51.963 --> 00:33:52.952
Doctor to Equinox.

00:33:53.097 --> 00:33:54.894
I've got their shield frequency.

00:33:54.966 --> 00:33:56.228
I'm transmitting it
to you now.

00:33:56.300 --> 00:33:57.426
They'll try to remodulate.

00:33:57.502 --> 00:33:58.434
Keep monitoring.

00:33:58.503 --> 00:34:00.198
Aye, sir.

00:34:00.271 --> 00:34:02.739
They've slowed
to one-quarter impulse.

00:34:02.807 --> 00:34:05.173
Prepare a tractor beam.

00:34:05.243 --> 00:34:06.733
They're launching
another torpedo.

00:34:06.811 --> 00:34:09.006
Full power
to the forward shields.

00:34:14.018 --> 00:34:16.213
Hull breach on Deck 4!

00:34:16.287 --> 00:34:17.754
How'd they get
through our shields?

00:34:18.890 --> 00:34:19.857
Hard about.

00:34:19.924 --> 00:34:21.221
Get us out of range.

00:34:21.292 --> 00:34:22.987
Remodulate the shields.

00:34:26.831 --> 00:34:27.923
They're retreating.

00:34:28.066 --> 00:34:28.930
Pursuit course.

00:34:29.067 --> 00:34:30.364
Maintain fire.

00:34:31.436 --> 00:34:33.199
They took out the weapons array!

00:34:33.271 --> 00:34:34.203
Tuvok?

00:34:34.272 --> 00:34:36.263
I've been rotating
the shield frequency

00:34:36.340 --> 00:34:37.568
every ten seconds.

00:34:39.243 --> 00:34:40.710
We've lost impulse engines.

00:34:40.778 --> 00:34:41.836
We're being hailed.

00:34:41.913 --> 00:34:43.403
It's Ransom.

00:34:44.615 --> 00:34:46.845
Put him through.

00:34:46.918 --> 00:34:50.945
Captain, I'm prepared
to surrender the Equinox,

00:34:51.022 --> 00:34:52.683
but I'm no longer in command.

00:34:52.757 --> 00:34:55.590
Max decided to stage
a little mutiny,

00:34:55.660 --> 00:34:56.957
but I think I can stop him.

00:34:57.028 --> 00:34:58.359
I've isolated
transporter control.

00:34:58.429 --> 00:34:59.953
I can beam all of us to Voyager.

00:35:00.098 --> 00:35:03.067
You might want to have
some guards standing by.

00:35:03.134 --> 00:35:05.227
Not everyone here is going
to be happy to see you.

00:35:08.206 --> 00:35:09.434
Proceed.

00:35:10.608 --> 00:35:11.802
Ma'am?

00:35:11.876 --> 00:35:13.867
He's still a Starfleet Captain.

00:35:13.945 --> 00:35:16.846
He may have forgotten that
for a while,

00:35:16.914 --> 00:35:19.246
but I believe him.

00:35:25.156 --> 00:35:27.488
Someone's trying to beam us off.

00:35:27.558 --> 00:35:28.923
Force fields!

00:35:28.993 --> 00:35:31.120
They're deflecting
our targeting scanners.

00:35:31.195 --> 00:35:34.096
Then beam the others to Voyager,
yourself included.

00:35:34.165 --> 00:35:35.826
I'll take care of Max.

00:35:37.468 --> 00:35:38.833
Aye, sir.

00:35:38.903 --> 00:35:43.431
Computer, give me access
to the shield grid.

00:35:53.184 --> 00:35:55.175
Well...

00:35:55.253 --> 00:35:57.118
I see you've
made yourself at home.

00:35:57.188 --> 00:35:58.177
What are you doing here?

00:35:58.256 --> 00:35:59.655
Taking back my Sick Bay.

00:35:59.724 --> 00:36:00.816
Stop where you are.

00:36:00.892 --> 00:36:02.154
I've planted photonic charges

00:36:02.226 --> 00:36:03.625
throughout
these holo-projectors.

00:36:03.694 --> 00:36:06.185
With one command sequence,
I can blow out your entire...

00:36:06.264 --> 00:36:07.629
Computer, delete
the Equinox EMH.

00:36:11.469 --> 00:36:13.334
The Doctor's not
transmitting anymore.

00:36:13.404 --> 00:36:14.735
Burke to Doctor.
Report.

00:36:14.805 --> 00:36:17.501
I'm afraid your physician's
no longer on call.

00:36:18.976 --> 00:36:20.170
Max, this is the Captain.

00:36:20.244 --> 00:36:21.438
I've dropped the shield grid

00:36:21.512 --> 00:36:23.810
everywhere except the Bridge
and my current location.

00:36:23.881 --> 00:36:25.712
The vital systems are exposed.

00:36:25.783 --> 00:36:29.378
I suggest you beam to Voyager
while you still can.

00:36:31.756 --> 00:36:32.916
The core is overloading.

00:36:33.024 --> 00:36:34.651
We've got to get out of here.

00:36:34.725 --> 00:36:35.885
Where? Voyager's brig?

00:36:35.960 --> 00:36:37.689
It's better
than being vaporized.

00:36:37.762 --> 00:36:39.491
We still have
a working shuttle.

00:36:39.564 --> 00:36:41.327
The Shuttle Bay's
two decks down!

00:36:41.399 --> 00:36:42.388
Sir, the aliens!

00:36:42.466 --> 00:36:43.558
We'll make it.

00:36:58.716 --> 00:36:59.740
This way.

00:37:16.400 --> 00:37:19.130
There's only one life sign left.

00:37:19.203 --> 00:37:21.068
It's Ransom.

00:37:25.376 --> 00:37:26.809
Captain.

00:37:26.877 --> 00:37:28.902
Things didn't work out
exactly as I planned,

00:37:29.046 --> 00:37:30.911
but you've got everyone
worth getting.

00:37:30.982 --> 00:37:33.109
We're beaming you out of there.

00:37:33.184 --> 00:37:35.015
This ship is about to explode.

00:37:35.086 --> 00:37:37.247
I've got to put some distance
between us.

00:37:37.321 --> 00:37:38.788
I've accessed helm control.

00:37:38.856 --> 00:37:42.019
You can set auto-navigation
and then transport to Voyager.

00:37:42.093 --> 00:37:43.617
There's no time!

00:37:43.694 --> 00:37:46.185
You've got a fine crew, Captain.

00:37:46.264 --> 00:37:49.199
Promise me you'll get 'em home.

00:37:50.268 --> 00:37:51.462
I promise.

00:38:59.603 --> 00:39:02.265
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:39:02.340 --> 00:39:04.240
With the Equinox destroyed,

00:39:04.308 --> 00:39:06.708
the aliens have withdrawn
to their realm.

00:39:06.777 --> 00:39:08.711
I've reinstated Chakotay,

00:39:08.779 --> 00:39:11.339
and we've set a course
for home.

00:39:11.415 --> 00:39:13.815
Good as new.

00:39:13.884 --> 00:39:16.648
I'd like you to regenerate
for the next few hours.

00:39:16.721 --> 00:39:18.484
It'll help stabilize
your cortical array.

00:39:18.556 --> 00:39:19.488
Understood.

00:39:19.557 --> 00:39:22.890
Regarding the...

00:39:22.993 --> 00:39:25.791
unpleasantness
aboard the Equinox,

00:39:25.863 --> 00:39:28.058
I hope you don't
think less of me.

00:39:28.132 --> 00:39:30.259
Your program was altered.

00:39:30.334 --> 00:39:31.801
It's quite
disconcerting to know

00:39:31.869 --> 00:39:33.097
that all someone has to do

00:39:33.170 --> 00:39:35.604
is flick a switch
to turn me into Mr. Hyde.

00:39:35.673 --> 00:39:37.538
Perhaps you should
enhance your program

00:39:37.608 --> 00:39:38.802
with security protocols.

00:39:38.876 --> 00:39:41.106
It will prevent such
tampering in the future.

00:39:41.178 --> 00:39:42.338
Good thinking.

00:39:42.413 --> 00:39:44.244
When I'm done regenerating,
I will assist you.

00:39:44.315 --> 00:39:45.873
Thanks.

00:39:45.950 --> 00:39:48.475
You were off-key.

00:39:48.552 --> 00:39:49.541
I beg your pardon?

00:39:49.620 --> 00:39:52.521
"My Darling Clementine,"
third verse, second measure.

00:39:52.590 --> 00:39:53.682
That's impossible.

00:39:53.758 --> 00:39:58.286
Your vocal modulations
deviated by 0.30 deci-hertz.

00:39:58.362 --> 00:40:00.796
I can assist you
with that as well.

00:40:00.865 --> 00:40:02.457
Really?

00:40:02.533 --> 00:40:06.799
Holodeck 2,
tomorrow, 1600 hours.

00:40:06.871 --> 00:40:08.896
Just you, me...

00:40:08.973 --> 00:40:12.136
and a tuning fork.

00:40:12.209 --> 00:40:14.404
I look forward to it.

00:40:22.186 --> 00:40:24.654
The last time
we welcomed you aboard,

00:40:24.722 --> 00:40:26.781
you took advantage of our trust.

00:40:26.857 --> 00:40:29.257
You betrayed this crew.

00:40:29.326 --> 00:40:32.625
I won't make that mistake again.

00:40:32.696 --> 00:40:35.187
Noah Lessing, Marla Gilmore,

00:40:35.266 --> 00:40:38.793
James Morrow, Brian
Sofin, Angelo Tassoni,

00:40:38.869 --> 00:40:41.133
you are hereby stripped of rank.

00:40:41.205 --> 00:40:44.641
You'll be expected to serve
as crewmen on this vessel.

00:40:44.708 --> 00:40:47.233
Your privileges will be limited,

00:40:47.311 --> 00:40:49.802
and you'll serve
under close supervision

00:40:49.880 --> 00:40:51.905
for as long as I deem fit.

00:40:51.982 --> 00:40:55.611
This time, you'll
have to earn our trust.

00:40:55.686 --> 00:40:57.779
Dismissed.

00:41:02.960 --> 00:41:05.258
Repairs?

00:41:05.329 --> 00:41:06.921
Coming along.

00:41:13.537 --> 00:41:15.300
How's the crew?

00:41:15.372 --> 00:41:18.000
A lot of frayed nerves.

00:41:23.013 --> 00:41:25.709
Neelix is organizing
a potluck...

00:41:25.783 --> 00:41:28.081
to help boost morale.

00:41:28.152 --> 00:41:31.553
Will I see you there?

00:41:31.622 --> 00:41:33.681
I'm replicating the salad.

00:41:33.757 --> 00:41:36.089
I'll bring the croutons.

00:41:39.763 --> 00:41:41.390
Chakotay...

00:41:52.376 --> 00:41:54.310
you know...

00:41:58.048 --> 00:41:59.982
you may have had good reason

00:42:00.084 --> 00:42:02.780
to stage a little mutiny
of your own.

00:42:06.357 --> 00:42:09.383
The thought had occurred to me,

00:42:09.460 --> 00:42:13.021
but that would have
been crossing the line.

00:42:16.600 --> 00:42:19.194
Will you look at that.

00:42:26.710 --> 00:42:30.874
All these years,
all these battles.

00:42:30.948 --> 00:42:34.406
This thing's never
fallen down before.

00:42:42.927 --> 00:42:46.055
Let's put it back up
where it belongs.
